**Takeaway:** Google Ads gained ~13.4 points of share (54.4% → 67.8%), funded mostly by a Meta pullback of ~12.4 points. Reddit stayed small and roughly flat in dollars, so its share drifted down slightly. Total spend grew ~19.7% ($9,892.11 → $11,844.59), so this was reallocation-plus-increase, not just a static pie.

**Caveats:**
- The tool reports relative windows (last/prior week) against a 2026-10-30 anchor, not exact calendar dates, so I can't state day boundaries precisely.
- One week of spend reallocation is directional only; worth checking whether the Google increase was paired with a deliberate budget change or a performance/automation shift before treating it as a trend.
